{"title":"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(De_Moivre&#39;s_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (De Moivre's Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(The_Floor_Divisor_Method)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (The Floor Divisor Method)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the product of the nonreal roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a53cf6467bd46594418f67723a37f5fa13fa3cfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4-4x^3+6x^2-4x=2005.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"225\" height=\"18\" /> Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/e/dfe7403149819f2e9fd4e8e0a7e22c5aaea26ee3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor P\\rfloor.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"34\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The left-hand side of that <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equation\" title=\"Equation\">equation</a> is nearly equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/4/b8465c8931a1e52e9387a7c609652201e4dab9d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x - 1)^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"19\" />.  Thus, we add 1 to each side in order to complete the fourth power and get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/3/8438b305f7500c34e924de293929d676f562ee5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x - 1)^4 = 2006$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/a/6ea78ab025a46a9201473cb8c0fbbaca3b79df50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\sqrt[4]{2006}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" /> be the positive <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Real\">real</a> fourth root of 2006.  Then the roots of the above equation are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e7948a1cd93caf3ac067a087bca6e980201b678.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1 + i^n r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/3407db930df14feb625315ee85a743308f37788a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 0, 1, 2, 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />.  The two non-real members of this set are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/9/189260a52a1e302f29535add1ba6217c0eadd139.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + ir$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57f096aa2bccd1cc5744c1deff3758f1f959ea09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 - ir$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />.  Their product is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/0/3706841ec84329d25d7c72b3379fb9e059ac2cb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = 1 + r^2 = 1 + \\sqrt{2006}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"193\" height=\"18\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/7/677f70f4070a75f5f0cc667e0210d92007af37fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44^2 = 1936 &lt; 2006 &lt; 2025 = 45^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"255\" height=\"15\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/8/a185e0d0e4d0d8201b1cb2d745a36074c0c0d276.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor P \\rfloor = 1 + 44 = \\boxed{045}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"169\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Starting like before,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/2/b62a4f1f25202d49dae8944b319ff0b2373b9f7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-1)^4= 2006$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"19\" />\nThis time we apply differences of squares.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/3/90382217f57f0a45ac4a9505740d9dd8a8daab21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-1)^4-2006=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"19\" /> so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/b/ddb94f0d993941bbdc92ffc9f20676f4a57ac96f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$((x-1)^2+\\sqrt{2006})((x-1)^2 -\\sqrt{2006})=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"335\" height=\"21\" />\nIf you think of each part of the product as a quadratic, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76ece07f987d433ae09767122b8ae143e5b38871.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$((x-1)^2+\\sqrt{2006})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"21\" /> is bound to hold the two  non-real roots since the other definitely crosses the x-axis twice since it is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> translated down and right.\nTherefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the product of the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76ece07f987d433ae09767122b8ae143e5b38871.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$((x-1)^2+\\sqrt{2006})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"21\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/e/7ee2759f5bb9816b6228190210b7328923dbbe30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=1+\\sqrt{2006}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" /> so\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/8/a185e0d0e4d0d8201b1cb2d745a36074c0c0d276.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor P \\rfloor = 1 + 44 = \\boxed{045}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"169\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we don't see the fourth power, we can always factor the LHS to try to create a quadratic substitution. Checking, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> are both roots. Synthetic division gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/d/ccdf1fd6884cd44359a6f2075a52ae16d4328c85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^2-2x)(x^2-2x+2)=2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"238\" height=\"19\" />. We now have our quadratic substitution of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/1/681c2d6f00feceaeab8ee527c02d1a4cb3f76f93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x^2-2x+1=(x-1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"210\" height=\"19\" />, giving us\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/8/a38d848a52664dfa48dd2010ee4a8f9722eabcf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y-1)(y+1)=2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"172\" height=\"20\" />. From here we proceed as in Solution 1 to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/f/34f1faa8dbe67c9d70702635a0b0d723b41f7d40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{045}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Realizing that if we add 1 to both sides we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/b/48be7d88f2d45faa11f5027990fe20d9b0b300a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4-4x^3+6x^2-4x+1=2006$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"249\" height=\"16\" /> which can be factored as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/a/09a758c1fadc06fd992b52050980c5b4c333e29c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-1)^4=2006$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"19\" />. Then we can substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af2e5691ba4f99b8214facf133f0e95fafa5db4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> which leaves us with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ce7b33420a4d2f6e13a1284b4d57f0ca2ed0aee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^4=2006$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />. Now subtracting 2006 from both sides we get some difference of squares <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/31007b37fd8c5a0235ea90b1a2010b71dcd2d2a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^4-2006=0 \\rightarrow (y-\\sqrt[4]{2006})(y+\\sqrt[4]{2006})(y^2+\\sqrt{2006})=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"471\" height=\"21\" />. The question asks for the product of the complex roots so we only care about the last factor which is equal to zero. From there we can solve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55f5e436c475ba61680692316713e082b0c20772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2+\\sqrt{2006}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"123\" height=\"20\" />, we can substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af2e5691ba4f99b8214facf133f0e95fafa5db4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> giving us  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2bd3e2ff74c7efaa7377a3b3792e3bec0d3849b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-1)^2+\\sqrt{2006}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"172\" height=\"24\" />, expanding this we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/d/f2d801b1f722f478e8794b641bdd64dc76e2ae08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-2x+1+\\sqrt{2006}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"197\" height=\"18\" />. We know that the product of a quadratics roots is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/4/b84719dcd9659dc2554a5e6701617224a5af26b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{c}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"33\" /> which leaves us with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/6/5a6adfa181cd822ca5a7a198e0d38a82cba61923.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1+\\sqrt{2006}}{1}=1+\\sqrt{2006}\\approx\\boxed{045}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"257\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in solution 1, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/d/dedd8ecbbd4cfdff8c36e4fd777944330919dbe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-1)^4 = 2006$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"19\" />. Now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/b/adb99ce1c2a5ed6cce74c426e1b5d30dd3c79a90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-1=\\pm \\sqrt[4]{2006}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"21\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/4/a448663adbc045fe2af8b1bd1432af971d56f4fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = 1+\\sqrt[4]{2006}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"22\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/e/e9e04a8d8e6bbf1a3d00fb9fdf230f9ed6759074.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2 = 1-\\sqrt[4]{2006}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"19\" /> are the real roots of the equation. Multiplying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/a/9aa736943b8bc97d944b20887daa35db3e008b39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 x_2 = 1 - \\sqrt{2006}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"143\" height=\"19\" />. Now transforming the original function and using Vieta's formula, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/0/cd0986784bacfd92a1351ca0a768ff44d7e6fda2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4-4x^3+6x^2-4x-2005=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"249\" height=\"16\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/f/08ffe4b84ced68f117fd128ca0027f4776557bcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 x_2 x_3 x_4 = \\frac{-2005}{1} = -2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"224\" height=\"38\" />. We find that the product of the nonreal roots is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/2/e02ab42f7f0fb8ec4ab4ead243f24f3f80f4ddfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_3 x_4 = \\frac{-2005}{1-\\sqrt{2006}} \\approx 45.8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"202\" height=\"42\" /> and we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/f/34f1faa8dbe67c9d70702635a0b0d723b41f7d40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{045}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Note: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/2/442532897371e4df75324534e81fc3ad82b48fca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2005}{\\sqrt[4]{2006}-1}=\\frac{2005(1+\\sqrt[4]{2006})}{2005} = 1+\\sqrt[4]{2006}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"360\" height=\"45\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28De_Moivre.27s_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(De_Moivre's_Theorem)\">Solution 6 (De Moivre's Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (De Moivre&#39;s Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As all the other solutions, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/d/dedd8ecbbd4cfdff8c36e4fd777944330919dbe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-1)^4 = 2006$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"19\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030f2f69d7cc335aea90c0b89539dbcd57159f8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\sqrt[4]{2006}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/1/6910469b4dce40f0294f2092125df7c1ee76c8bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x= \\sqrt[4]{2006}(\\cos(\\frac{2\\pi(k)}{4}+i\\sin(\\frac{2\\pi(k)}{4}))+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"327\" height=\"39\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d164dd51c4a3ba53fcdd187c7bf57522ce6b3434.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=0,1,2,3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" />. The complex values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> are the ones where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/8/708012a3b381e8b4db3d4598c0f77952a0b3671f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i\\sin(\\frac{2\\pi(k)}{4})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"92\" height=\"39\" /> does not equal 0. These complex roots are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/e/ffed9c820030cd6da031a1a444b3a29697f85da9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+\\sqrt[4]{2006}(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/b/25b1bd6efe50549b1b218174714edbed50546668.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\sqrt[4]{2006}(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"21\" />. The product of these two nonreal roots is (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/e/ffed9c820030cd6da031a1a444b3a29697f85da9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+\\sqrt[4]{2006}(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"21\" />)(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/b/25b1bd6efe50549b1b218174714edbed50546668.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\sqrt[4]{2006}(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"21\" />) which is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/9/ec977c86d7e1ebb2833eeaa07eb3e478587c5d0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+\\sqrt {2006}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />. The floor of that value is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/f/34f1faa8dbe67c9d70702635a0b0d723b41f7d40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{045}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28The_Floor_Divisor_Method.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(The_Floor_Divisor_Method)\">Solution 7 (The Floor Divisor Method)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (The Floor Divisor Method)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Continue Solution 1 until we obtain the equation \\( (x-1)^4 = 2006 \\). Then, we see that \\( x = 1 \\pm \\sqrt[4]{2006} \\). While one could see the possible roots are \\( 1 \\pm \\sqrt[4]{2006} \\), and \\( 1 \\pm \\sqrt[4]{2006}i \\), and obtain 45, one could have also seen the product of all roots is \\( -2005 \\) through Vieta's. Then, the product of the two remaining real roots is \\( 1 - \\sqrt{2006} \\), and thus the wanted value is \\( \\left\\lfloor \\frac{-2005}{1 - \\sqrt{2006}} \\right\\rfloor \\) or \\( \\left\\lfloor \\frac{2005}{\\sqrt{2006} - 1} \\right\\rfloor \\), which through the divisor method is \\( \\left\\lfloor \\frac{2005}{\\lfloor \\sqrt{2006} - 1 \\rfloor} \\right\\rfloor +1 \\), or \\( \\left\\lfloor \\frac{2005}{43} \\right\\rfloor +1 \\), whose floor is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/f/34f1faa8dbe67c9d70702635a0b0d723b41f7d40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{045}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />. \n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p><p>The formal Floor Divisor Method states that for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37b0592d5856e34bd8b545b0ab6efcbf8c5edb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\lfloor a \\rfloor, \\quad B = \\lfloor b \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"20\" />, the floor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/084079bf1d54500f3c59257a7ec3467932b72ba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"34\" /> is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99c0b08eb9f9db1a9ef29c51f4ddeef917bbb6cf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lfloor a/b \\rfloor = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{A}{B} - \\frac{\\mathbf{1}_{(a \\bmod b) &lt; (A \\bmod B)}}{1} \\right\\rfloor\\]\" width=\"266\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>More informally, without the bolded 1 (conditional 1), \n</p><p>For all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37b0592d5856e34bd8b545b0ab6efcbf8c5edb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\lfloor a \\rfloor, \\quad B = \\lfloor b \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"20\" />, \n\\begin{array}{c} \\lfloor a/b \\rfloor =\n\\begin{cases} \n\\lfloor A/B \\rfloor &amp; \\text{if } a \\ge \\lfloor A/B \\rfloor \\cdot b \\\\[2mm]\n\\lfloor A/B \\rfloor - 1 &amp; \\text{if } a &lt; \\lfloor A/B \\rfloor \\cdot b\n\\end{cases} \\end{array}\n</p><p>As a problem to the reader, try to figure out why I simplified this formula above into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/9/1395bf573275cd84bb2ae51ff64560d4eb3f62e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor \\frac{a}{b} \\right\\rfloor +1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"65\" height=\"35\" /> for this problem, and when should and should not simplify to this form.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Video Solution\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LbHg1Su2Rmg\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LbHg1Su2Rmg</a>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I\" title=\"2005 AIME I\">2005 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2005\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016220358\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.046 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.067 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 450/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1786/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: